From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: integrate MST streams and negotiated lane bounds

Adapt Qualcomm's DisplayPort MST v7 series (1-35) and IRQ_HPD v8 bridge
contract to the Uke 7.3 native display profile. Preserve the SST DSC/FEC,
color, runtime-PM and failed-enable guards. Bound training by the actual
Type-C route, retain unchanged retimer routing on IRQ_HPD, and unwind
failed MST payload transactions without taking another stream down.

MST currently admits RGB 8-bpc SDR only; compressed/HDR MST is refused.
Four-lane training requires firmware-negotiated C/E; no pin force is added.

Sources and original authors:
MST v7: Yongxing Mou and Abhinav Kumar.
IRQ_HPD v8: Dmitry Baryshkov.
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260929-msm-dp-mst-v7-0-4b81473185e7@oss.qualcomm.com/
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024-hpd-irq-events-v8-0-6ee949e7a384@oss.qualcomm.com/
Original Qualcomm copyright and SPDX notices are retained in new files.
